+      </ul>
+      <t indent="0" pn="section-abstract-3">The requirements or rules of each service must be set through administrative policy mechanisms which are outside the scope of this document.  A differentiated services-compliant network node includes a classifier that selects packets based on the value of the DS field, along with buffer management and packet scheduling mechanisms capable of delivering the specific packet forwarding treatment indicated by the DS field value.  Setting of the DS field and conditioning of the temporal behavior of marked packets need only be performed at network boundaries and may vary in complexity.</t>
